{
  // @orb/client is browser code (the frontend cake tip: kit ← ui ← client). DOM libs + JSX on top
  // of the isomorphic base — mirrors packages/ui. Explicit include (was implicit-everything): the
  // package's own code PLUS the client-owned CT browser program the root aggregator excludes —
  // EVERY browser tsx under tests/client, matched by DIRECTORY not filename suffix (so a mis-named
  // helper can't fall through to the node aggregator and be checked without dom — D62 tsconfig-boundary
  // hardening) and the client-side CT provider stack (ct-data-providers.tsx — it imports @orb/client,
  // so it can NEVER be swept into ui's program: upward-cake; packages/ui/tsconfig.json includes only
  // ct-providers.tsx).
  //
  // #1228, the DOM-lib-leak defuse: ct-config-groups.ts is ct-data-providers.tsx's NON-`.tsx` sibling
  // (the "a non-component module beside ct-data-providers.tsx" its own header names) — it imports
  // every `@orb/client/features/*` config-group barrel, so it is DOM-coupled by the same transitive
  // chain, but being `.ts` (not `.tsx`) no directory-glob reach-back above claims it. It used to reach
  // this program's dom lib ONLY via the root aggregator's leaked `/// <reference lib="dom" />`
  // (scripts/probes/st-goldens/generate-goldens.ts); the root aggregator now excludes it explicitly.
  //
  // #1312 (2026-09-05): browser purity is NOT enforced by the base's `types: []` — that only
  // suppresses AUTO-inclusion of `@types/*`, and cannot suppress the `/// <reference types="node" />`
  // a DEPENDENCY .d.ts injects (measured: the type-only `import type { AppRouter } from "@orb/server"`
  // edge — 5 sites, sanctioned by dep-cruiser `client-no-backend-runtime` — reaches pino-std-serializers
  // and undici-types, which reference `node`, so `Buffer.from("x")` typechecks clean here). The real
  // enforcers are dep-cruiser `client-no-backend-runtime` (runtime import edges), biome
  // `correctness/noNodejsModules` (node:* import form) and biome `style/noRestrictedGlobals` (bare
  // globals — Buffer/setImmediate/global/…, biome.json's last override).
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    // VITE is this package's resolver, so it stays on the bundler pair while the base went nodenext
    // (tsx-shedding stage 4). Not a weakening: node-strict resolution is a SUBSET of what vite accepts,
    // and the shared packages (kit/contracts) are checked under nodenext by their own programs.
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    // `esnext.disposable` mirrors tsconfig.base.json's lib (node-26 adoption program §1.1) — this array
    // OVERRIDES the base's, so the entry must be repeated here. (§5 rules ui/client have zero
    // disposal-shaped sites today; the lib stays uniform so a program never silently loses the typing.)
    "lib": ["es2025", "esnext.disposable", "esnext.temporal", "dom", "dom.iterable"],
    "jsx": "react-jsx"
  },
  // `../../platform.d.ts` = the root ambient pair's second half (node-26 adoption program §1.2) — see
  // tsconfig.base.json's include note: this array overrides the base's, which carries both.
  "include": [
    "src",
    "vite.config.ts",
    "../../reset.d.ts",
    "../../platform.d.ts",
    "../../tests/client/**/*.tsx",
    "../../tests/support/ct/ct-data-providers.tsx",
    "../../tests/support/ct/ct-config-groups.ts"
  ]
}
